- data = ethnicity_data
%main.community-map-page
  %h2.mb-2 Los Angeles Area Ethnic Groups
  %p.community-map-intro
    Where people of each ethnic group live, from the 2020 Census.
    Pick a group to see it on the big map, or filter by region of origin.
  .community-map-layout
    %section.map-panel#map-panel{ aria: { label: 'Selected group' }, data: { group: data.to_json, year: 2020, base_path: ethnicities_path, heat_intensity: 0.6 } }
      %h3.map-title
        %span.map-group-name= @ethnicity.name
      %p.map-total
        %strong#map-total-count= number_with_delimiter(@ethnicity.people)
        people in the Los Angeles area identified as
        %span.map-group-name= @ethnicity.name
        in the 2020 Census
      .big-map
      %details.map-table{ open: true }
        %summary
          By county
        %table.table.table-sm
          %thead
            %tr
              %th County
              %th.text-end People
          %tbody#map-table-body
    %section.footprint-wall{ aria: { label: 'Ethnic groups' } }
      -# Cached until the data or outline change. The selected card is marked by JavaScript.
      - cache ['ethnicity-footprints', EthnicityCount.count, EthnicityCount.maximum(:id), File.mtime(Rails.root.join('config/la_area_outline.json')).to_i] do
        = render 'shared/footprint_wall', cards: ethnicity_cards, categories: Ethnicity::CATEGORIES & Ethnicity.distinct.pluck(:category),
                 key_text: 'Blue dots are the census tracts where a group lives; bigger dots mean more people.'
  .map-notes
    %p.map-contact
      Know a community we're missing, or see something that looks wrong? Email
      = succeed('.') do
        = contact_email_link
    %p
      People could identify with more than one group, and each group counts everyone who listed it,
      so the groups add up to more than the area's population.
      Hispanic or Latino origin (for example Mexican or Salvadoran) is a separate question from race,
      so someone can appear in both a Latin American group and another group, such as Aztec or Maya.
    %p
      To protect privacy, the Census Bureau only reports a group in a census tract where at least 22 people belong to it,
      and adds small random changes to every count.
      Totals are for each county, so they include people in tracts too small to be shown on the map.
      Broad groups like "European" or "East Asian" are left out in favor of the specific groups within them.
    %p
      Source:
      = link_to('U.S. Census Bureau, 2020 Census Detailed Demographic and Housing Characteristics File A', 'https://www.census.gov/data/tables/2023/dec/2020-census-detailed-dhc-a.html', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener')
      for Los Angeles, Orange, Ventura, Riverside, and San Bernardino counties.
      County outlines from the
      = succeed('.') do
        = link_to('California Department of Technology', 'https://gis.data.ca.gov/datasets/CDT::california-county-boundaries-and-identifiers', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener')
